{"path":"numeric/complex/arg","title":"std::arg(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>arg<small>(std::complex)</small>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/arg","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"The additional overloads are not required to be provided exactly as (A,B). They only need to be sufficient to ensure that for their argument num:","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br>T &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-h\">\n<td> <div><a href=\"#Notes\">Additional overloads</a> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n<tbody class=\"t-dcl-rev t-dcl-rev-num\"><tr class=\"t-dcl-rev-aux\">\n<td></td>\n<td rowspan=\"142\">(A)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx23\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> f <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> f <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> f <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx23\">(until C++23)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> FloatingPoint <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br>FloatingPoint<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span> FloatingPoint f <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Integer <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;arg<span class=\"br0\">(</span> Integer i <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (B) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Calculates the phase angle (in radians) of the complex number <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>.</div>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx11\"><td>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">A,B)</span> Additional overloads are provided for all integer and floating-point types, which are treated as complex numbers with zero imaginary component.</div>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> f\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> floating-point value\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> i\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> integer value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan2\"><span class=\"kw1347\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atan2</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/imag2\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">imag</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/real2\"><span class=\"kw2712\">std::<span class=\"me2\">real</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. If no errors occur, this is the phase angle of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> in the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−π; π]</span>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">A)</span> Zero if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code> is positive or +0, <span class=\"texhtml\">π</span> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code> is negative or -0, NaN otherwise.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">B)</span> Zero if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">i</span></code> is non-negative, <span class=\"texhtml\">π</span> if it is negative.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The additional overloads are not required to be provided exactly as <span class=\"t-v\">(A,B)</span>. They only need to be sufficient to ensure that for their argument <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">num</span></code>:\n</p>\n<ul><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">num</span></code> has a <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-until-cxx23\"><span>standard</span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx23\">(until C++23)</span></span></span> floating-point type <code>T</code>, then <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>num<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> has the same effect as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>num<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li><li> Otherwise, if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">num</span></code> has an integer type, then <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>num<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> has the same effect as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>num<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> \n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z1<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z3<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z4<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z5<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> f <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>.<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z1<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z3 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z4 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z4<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z5 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z5<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" \"</span>\n                 <span class=\"st0\">\"(the other side of the cut)<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> f <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"phase angle of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">arg</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>phase angle of (1,0) is 0\nphase angle of (0,0) is 0\nphase angle of (0,1) is 1.5708\nphase angle of (-1,0) is 3.14159\nphase angle of (-1,-0) is -3.14159 (the other side of the cut)\nphase angle of 1 is 0\nphase angle of -1 is 3.14159</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/abs\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>abs<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the magnitude of a complex number <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/polar\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>polar</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs a complex number from magnitude and phase angle <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan2</span><span>atan2f</span><span>atan2l</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  arc tangent, using signs to determine quadrants <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/atan2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan2<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/atan2\">std::atan2</a></span> to a valarray and a value <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/carg\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>carg</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::arg(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: until C++23, since C++23. Calculates the phase angle (in radians) of the complex number z."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z, f, i"},{"label":"Return value","note":"std::atan2(std::imag(z), std::real(z)). If no errors occur, this is the phase angle of z in the interval [−π; π]."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The additional overloads are not required to be provided exactly as (A,B). They only need to be sufficient to ensure that for their argument num:"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"abs(std::complex)","note":"returns the magnitude of a complex number"},{"label":"polar","note":"constructs a complex number from magnitude and phase angle"},{"label":"atan2, atan2f, atan2l","note":"arc tangent, using signs to determine quadrants"},{"label":"atan2(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::atan2 to a valarray and a value"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++23"],"wordCount":461,"codeBlockCount":2}
